@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`

-- ===========================================================================
-- s 66(c).  Lines 2460-2478.
--
--   (ג) אלה ההוראות שיחולו לגבי החישוב הנפרד:
--   (1)  הזכאות לניכויים, לזיכויים ולנקודות זיכוי לפי סעיפים 34, 35, 36, 45א,
--        47, 47א ו־121א, ההטבה במס על פי סעיף 10 וההנחה במס על פי סעיף 11
--        יהיו לכל אחד מבני הזוג;
--   (1א) בן זוג רשאי, אף אם לבן זוגו אין הכנסה מיגיעה אישית, לבקש חישוב נפרד
--        על הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית, ויהיה זכאי, כנגד המס החל על הכנסתו זו,
--        לנקודות זיכוי כאמור בפסקאות (4) או (5);
--   (2)  לענין זכאות לפי סעיף 37 של יחיד מוטב, כהגדרתו באותו סעיף, תובא בחשבון
--        ½ נקודת זיכוי בלבד, ולא תהא זכאות לנקודות זיכוי לפי סעיפים 38 ו־39;
--   (3)  זכאות לנקודות קיצבה על פי סעיף 40(א) תהא רק לבן הזוג הרשום;
--   (4)  האשה תהא זכאית ל־½ נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 36א, ובנוסף וכנגד המס החל על
--        הכנסתה מיגיעה אישית – לנקודות זיכוי בעד ילדיה כלהלן:
--     (א) [the table: see `s 66(c)(4)(a)` below] ...; לעניין זה ולעניין פסקה
--         (5), ”שנת לידה“ ו”שנת בגרות“ – כהגדרתן בסעיף 40(ב)(3);
--     (א1) על אף האמור בפסקת משנה (א), אמו של ילד תהיה זכאית לבחור אם נקודת
--         זיכוי אחת מתוך נקודות הזיכוי שלהן היא זכאית כאמור באותה פסקה, בשנת
--         הלידה, תובא בחשבון בשנת המס שבה נולד הילד או בשנת המס שלאחריה;
--     (ב) (נמחקה); (ג) (נמחקה); (ד) (פקעה);
--        לענין זה, ”שנת לידה“ ו”שנת בגרות“ – כהגדרתם בסעיף 40(ב)(3);
--   (4א) בחישוב המס של אישה שנישאה לאלמן יובאו בחשבון נקודות זיכוי בעד כל
--        אחד מילדיו, כאמור בפסקה (4);
--   (5)  הגבר יהא זכאי, כנגד המס החל על הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית, לנקודות זיכוי
--        בעד כל אחד מילדיו, כלהלן: (א) ... (ב) ... (ג) ...
--   (5א) (פקעה);
--   (6)  בחישוב המס של גבר שנישא לאלמנה יובאו בחשבון נקודות זיכוי בעד כל אחד
--        מילדיה, כאמור בפסקה (5).
--
-- WHAT IS COUNTED HERE AND WHAT IS NOT.  This module counts the credit points
-- that s 66(c) itself gives or cuts: one half under s 36A for the woman
-- ((c)(4)), one half under s 37 where s 37 would give one ((c)(2)), and the
-- children's points ((c)(4), (4A), (5), (6)).  The points under ss 34, 35 and
-- 36 that (c)(1) gives each spouse are counted by those sections (IL-01) for
-- the spouse alone, and are not added here.  The value of a credit point
-- (s 33A, IL-01) and the tax on income from personal exertion (s 121 ff.,
-- IL-03) are GIVENs of the one rule that converts points into a credit.
--
-- TAX YEARS (version 0.2.0, 02-V4).  Every rule here that takes the couple,
-- or a tax year, refuses a year before 2024 (A1, ito66-tax-years.l4).  The
-- rules that take no year (the tables by age, what (c) does with each
-- provision, the set-off against the tax) state the deposited text; so does
-- `a woman and a man:`, a fact about the couple, not a provision.
--
-- SECTION 48A (version 0.2.0, 02-R2; assumed, not ruled: the lead's choice).
-- (c)(4) gives the woman half a point "לפי סעיף 36א", under s 36A, which is in
-- Part C, Chapter Three (heading at line 1559).  s 48A, line 1811, lets the
-- Minister provide that "הוראות פרק זה לענין זיכויים ... לא יחולו על עובד זר",
-- and Regulations of 5775-2014 are noted at line 1812 but are not in the
-- source bundle.  Row IL-01 declines s 36A for a foreign worker in the words
-- "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this
-- model" (its ito-s34-s36-s36a-credits.l4, rules `section 48A and the
-- regulations made under it are not encoded in this model` and `section 36A
-- applies to`: lines 99-103 and 191-197 at commons 3f7d673, 115-116 and 207
-- in IL-01's v0.2.0 working tree of 2026-10-08, which applies the refusal
-- from tax year 2002 in its year-aware rules, so in every year this row
-- answers); this
-- row declines the half point in the same words, so the two rows agree.  The
-- children's points of (c)(4)-(6) are s 66's own, and s 66 is in Part D,
-- Chapter Three (heading at line 2437), outside "פרק זה"; s 48A does not reach
-- them on its words, and they are answered.  The half point under s 37 in
-- (c)(2) turns on the caller's s 37 answer, which already carries s 48A.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 66(c) — when it governs a spouse's calculation`

-- (c)(1A): "אף אם לבן זוגו אין הכנסה מיגיעה אישית" puts no condition on the
-- partner.  Either spouse may make the request; the same input records the
-- (a)(1) claim and the (1A) request.  READING (fork F8): (1A) sits in (c), not
-- in (a), so the (d) gate on subsection (a) does not reach it.
@ref s 66(c)(1A), line 2462; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(c)(1A) — a separate calculation of income from personal exertion is requested by the` which `in` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (    `the taxable income from personal exertion of` `the spouse` GREATER THAN 0
         AND `the spouse`'s `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion`)
    WHERE `the spouse` MEANS `the particulars of the` which `in` couple

-- (c) states "the provisions that apply regarding the separate calculation".
-- They govern both spouses' calculations once a separate calculation is
-- made under (a)(1) ("יהיו לכל אחד מבני הזוג", "האשה", "הגבר"), and the
-- requesting spouse's calculation under (1A).
@ref s 66(c) chapeau, line 2460; (a)(1), line 2456; (c)(1A), line 2462; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(c) — governs the calculation of the` which `in` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (    `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` couple
         OR  `s 66(c)(1A) — a separate calculation of income from personal exertion is requested by the` which `in` couple)

§ `Section 66(c)(1)-(4) — the entitlements, provision by provision`

DECLARE `A provision section 66(c) speaks of` IS ONE OF
    `section 34`
    `section 35`
    `section 36`
    `section 45A`
    `section 47`
    `section 47A`
    `section 121A`
    `the tax benefit under section 10`
    `the tax reduction under section 11`
    `section 37`
    `section 38`
    `section 39`
    `section 40(a)`
    `section 36A`
    `a provision section 66(c) does not name` HAS `the provision` IS A STRING

DECLARE `What section 66(c) does with the provision` IS ONE OF
    `each of the spouses has the entitlement`             -- (c)(1)
    `one half credit point only`                          -- (c)(2), s 37
    `there is no entitlement`                             -- (c)(2), ss 38, 39
    `the registered spouse alone has the entitlement`     -- (c)(3)
    `the woman has one half credit point`                 -- (c)(4), s 36A

-- READING (fork F10): for a provision (c) does not name (ss 39A, 39B, 40A-40D,
-- 44, 45, 46, ...), s 66 says nothing, and whether a spouse in a separate
-- calculation has it turns on that provision's own words.  Not in this slice.
@ref s 66(c)(1)-(4), lines 2461-2465
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 66(c) does not say how a provision it does not name applies in a separate calculation` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 66(c) does not say how a provision it does not name applies in a separate calculation"

@ref s 66(c)(1)-(4), lines 2461-2465
GIVEN p IS A `A provision section 66(c) speaks of`
GIVETH A `What section 66(c) does with the provision`
`s 66(c) — in a separate calculation, as to` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `section 34`                         THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 35`                         THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 36`                         THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 45A`                        THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 47`                         THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 47A`                        THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 121A`                       THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `the tax benefit under section 10`   THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `the tax reduction under section 11` THEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 37`                         THEN `one half credit point only`
    WHEN `section 38`                         THEN `there is no entitlement`
    WHEN `section 39`                         THEN `there is no entitlement`
    WHEN `section 40(a)`                      THEN `the registered spouse alone has the entitlement`
    WHEN `section 36A`                        THEN `the woman has one half credit point`
    WHEN `a provision section 66(c) does not name` `the name`
                                              THEN `s 66(c) does not say how a provision it does not name applies in a separate calculation`

§ `Section 66(c)(4)-(6) — the woman and the man`

-- READING (fork F9): (c)(4) gives to "האשה" and (c)(5) to "הגבר", with the
-- definite article: the paragraphs are written for a couple of a woman and
-- a man.  For a couple of the same sex the text does not say which paragraph
-- governs whom, and this encoding declines.
@ref s 66(c)(4)-(6), lines 2465-2478
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 66(c)(4)-(6) speak of the woman and the man of a couple; this encoding does not decide them for a couple of the same sex` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 66(c)(4)-(6) speak of the woman and the man of a couple; this encoding does not decide them for a couple of the same sex"

@ref s 66(c)(4)-(6), lines 2465-2478
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a woman and a man:` couple MEANS
    NOT (couple's `the registered spouse`'s `sex` EQUALS couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`'s `sex`)

§§ `Section 66(c)(4)(a) and (5) — the tables`

-- s 40(b)(3), lines 1644-1645, incorporated by s 66(c)(4)(a) (line 2466)
-- and again by the unnumbered line after (c)(4)(d) (line 2471, a repetition
-- the consolidation carries; both say the same thing):
--     ”שנת לידה“ – שנת המס שבה נולד הילד;
--     ”שנת בגרות“ – שנת המס שבה מלאו לילד שמונה עשרה שנים.
-- So in a tax year the child "turns" (tax year - tax year of birth): 0 in the
-- year of birth, 18 in the year of majority.  Every band of both tables is
-- stated in those terms ("בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שלוש שנים", ...).
@ref s 40(b)(3), lines 1644-1645, by s 66(c)(4)(a), line 2466, and line 2471
GIVEN `the child`    IS A `A child, for section 66`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age the child` `the child` `turns in tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `the tax year` MINUS `the child`'s `tax year of birth`

-- (c)(4)(a), in the source's own order.  The arms are disjoint, so the order
-- decides nothing; it is kept so the table reads against line 2466.
--   "2½ נקודות זיכוי בעד כל אחד מילדיה בשנת לידתו,
--    ו־½ נקודת זיכוי בעד כל אחד מילדיה בשנת בגרותו,
--    4½ נקודות זיכוי ... החל בשנת המס שלאחר שנת לידתו ועד לשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שנתיים,
--    3½ נקודות זיכוי ... בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שלוש שנים,
--    2½ נקודות זיכוי ... בשנות המס שבהן מלאו לו ארבע שנים וחמש שנים,
--    ושתי נקודות זיכוי ... החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים ועד לשנת המס שקדמה לשנת בגרותו"
-- A child outside every band (not yet born, or past the year of majority)
-- earns nothing under the paragraph.
@ref s 66(c)(4)(a), line 2466
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4)(a) — the woman's credit points for a child who turns` `the age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 0                              THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 18                             THEN 0.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 1 AND `the age` AT MOST 2    THEN 4.5
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 3                              THEN 3.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 4 AND `the age` AT MOST 5    THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 6 AND `the age` AT MOST 17   THEN 2
        OTHERWISE                                                 0

-- (c)(5)(a)-(c), in the source's order.  (5) has no year-of-majority row:
-- the last band ends with the year before it.
--   (א) 2½ נקודות זיכוי בשנת לידתו של הילד;
--   (ב) 4½ ... החל בשנת המס שלאחר לידתו ועד לשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שנתיים,
--       3½ ... בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שלוש שנים, ו־2½ ... בשנות המס שבהן מלאו
--       לו ארבע שנים וחמש שנים;
--   (ג) נקודת זיכוי אחת ... החל בשנת המס שבה מלאו לו שש שנים ועד לשנת המס
--       שקדמה לשנת בגרותו;
@ref s 66(c)(5)(a)-(c), lines 2474-2476
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(5) — the man's credit points for a child who turns` `the age` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 0                              THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 1 AND `the age` AT MOST 2    THEN 4.5
        IF   `the age` EQUALS 3                              THEN 3.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 4 AND `the age` AT MOST 5    THEN 2.5
        IF   `the age` AT LEAST 6 AND `the age` AT MOST 17   THEN 1
        OTHERWISE                                                 0

-- (c)(4)(a1): the mother may move ONE of her birth-year points into the
-- following tax year.  READING (fork F11): the election is the mother's
-- ("אמו של ילד"), so it does not reach a step-mother's points under (4A).
--
-- FORK F19 (02-E4).  A child born before 2024, in practice in 2023, the
-- election set, asked of tax year 2024: the point moved is one "מתוך נקודות
-- הזיכוי שלהן היא זכאית כאמור באותה פסקה, בשנת הלידה", and the year of birth is
-- governed by a text this row does not hold (A1).
-- (i) The 2024 text governs the 2024 calculation and says where the point
-- lands: 4½ + 1 = 5½ (the behaviour of versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0).
-- (ii) Whether the mother could elect in the year of birth, and had a point
-- to move, is that year's law, which this row does not hold: declined.
-- RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG; BACKLOG IL-38, version 0.3.0): one
-- named switch, default (ii), reading (i) kept by name and tested.  The input
-- carries no year of election, so the facts cannot tell the readings apart.
-- A child born from 2024 on is not reached: both readings answer alike.
-- NOTES.md section 4.
DECLARE `A reading of section 66(c)(4)(a1) for a child born before 2024` IS ONE OF
    -- (i)
    `an election for a child born before 2024 is carried by the text of the year of the calculation`
    -- (ii), the default
    `an election for a child born before 2024 is declined`

@ref s 66(c)(4)(a1), line 2467; fork F19; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(c)(4)(a1) for a child born before 2024`
`section 66(c)(4)(a1) — the reading this row takes for an election for a child born before 2024` MEANS
    `an election for a child born before 2024 is declined`

@ref s 66(c)(4)(a1), line 2467; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F19
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024` MEANS
    REFUSE "the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024"

@ref s 66(c)(4)(a), (a1), lines 2466-2467; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F19
GIVEN `the child`    IS A `A child, for section 66`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
      r              IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(4)(a1) for a child born before 2024`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `the child` `in tax year` `the tax year` `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` r MEANS
    `in tax year` `the tax year` `, the answer is`
        (BRANCH
            IF   `elected` AND `the age` EQUALS 0
            THEN `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the woman's credit points for a child who turns` `the age` MINUS 1
            IF   `elected` AND `the age` EQUALS 1 AND `born before the text`
            THEN CONSIDER r
                 WHEN `an election for a child born before 2024 is carried by the text of the year of the calculation`
                 THEN `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the woman's credit points for a child who turns` `the age` PLUS 1
                 WHEN `an election for a child born before 2024 is declined`
                 THEN `the text of section 66 this encoding holds does not decide a birth-year credit point elected for a child born before 2024`
            IF   `elected` AND `the age` EQUALS 1
            THEN `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the woman's credit points for a child who turns` `the age` PLUS 1
            OTHERWISE `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the woman's credit points for a child who turns` `the age`)
    WHERE
        `the age` MEANS `the age the child` `the child` `turns in tax year` `the tax year`
        `elected` MEANS `the child`'s `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year`
        `born before the text` MEANS
            `the child`'s `tax year of birth` LESS THAN `the first tax year the deposited text of section 66 governs`

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 and 0.2.0, by its old name, now at the reading
-- the switch names.
@ref s 66(c)(4)(a), (a1), lines 2466-2467; the switch above
GIVEN `the child`    IS A `A child, for section 66`
      `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `the child` `in tax year` `the tax year` MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `the child` `in tax year` `the tax year`
        `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `section 66(c)(4)(a1) — the reading this row takes for an election for a child born before 2024`

§§ `Section 66(c)(4)(b)-(d) and (5A) — spent`

-- Lines 2468-2470 and 2477.  Stubs, so the paragraph has no silent gap; no
-- operative content.  What the expired paragraphs said is not in the source.
GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(c)(4)(b) — deleted` MEANS "(נמחקה)"

GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(c)(4)(c) — deleted` MEANS "(נמחקה)"

GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(c)(4)(d) — expired` MEANS "(פקעה)"

GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(c)(5A) — expired` MEANS "(פקעה)"

§§ `Section 66(c)(4), (4A), (5), (6) — whose children`

@ref s 66(c)(4), (5), lines 2465, 2473
GIVEN which      IS A `Which spouse`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a child of the` which `:` `the child` MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `registered spouse`                       THEN `the child`'s `a child of the registered spouse`
    WHEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse` THEN `the child`'s `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse`

GIVEN which IS A `Which spouse`
GIVETH A `Which spouse`
`the partner of the` which MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `registered spouse`                       THEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
    WHEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse` THEN `registered spouse`

-- (4A) "אישה שנישאה לאלמן ... בעד כל אחד מילדיו" and (6) "גבר שנישא לאלמנה
-- ... בעד כל אחד מילדיה": the partner's own children count too, where the
-- partner was widowed when this marriage was made.  A child of both is
-- counted once.  READING (fork F12): only a WIDOWED partner's children; a
-- divorced partner's children from an earlier marriage are not reached.
@ref s 66(c)(4A), (6), lines 2472, 2478; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN which      IS A `Which spouse`
      couple     IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(c)(4A), (6) — a child of the widowed partner of the` which `in` couple `:` `the child` MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (    NOT `a child of the` which `:` `the child`
         AND (`the particulars of the partner of the` which `in` couple)'s `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted`
         AND `a child of the` (`the partner of the` which) `:` `the child`)

-- One child's points for one spouse, by that spouse's sex: (4)(a)-(a1) for
-- the woman's own child, (4)(a) through (4A) for a widower's child, (5) for
-- the man's own child and, through (6), for a widow's child.
-- Version 0.3.0: the reading of fork F19 is passed to (a1); the rule of the
-- old name, below, passes the switch.
@ref s 66(c)(4)-(6), lines 2465-2478; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F19
GIVEN which      IS A `Which spouse`
      couple     IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
      r          IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(4)(a1) for a child born before 2024`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` which `in` couple `for` `the child` `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` r MEANS
    `in tax year` `the year` `, the answer is`
        (CONSIDER `the spouse`'s `sex`
         WHEN `a woman` THEN BRANCH
                                 IF   `a child of the` which `:` `the child`
                                 THEN `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `the child` `in tax year` `the year` `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` r
                                 IF   `s 66(c)(4A), (6) — a child of the widowed partner of the` which `in` couple `:` `the child`
                                 THEN `s 66(c)(4)(a) — the woman's credit points for a child who turns` `the age`
                                 OTHERWISE 0
         WHEN `a man`   THEN IF   `a child of the` which `:` `the child`
                                  OR `s 66(c)(4A), (6) — a child of the widowed partner of the` which `in` couple `:` `the child`
                             THEN `s 66(c)(5) — the man's credit points for a child who turns` `the age`
                             ELSE 0)
    WHERE
        `the spouse` MEANS `the particulars of the` which `in` couple
        `the year`   MEANS couple's `tax year`
        `the age`    MEANS `the age the child` `the child` `turns in tax year` `the year`

@ref s 66(c)(4)-(6), lines 2465-2478; the switch of fork F19
GIVEN which      IS A `Which spouse`
      couple     IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` which `in` couple `for` `the child` MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` which `in` couple `for` `the child`
        `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `section 66(c)(4)(a1) — the reading this row takes for an election for a child born before 2024`

§§ `Section 66(c) — the credit points it gives a spouse`

DECLARE `Credit points under section 66(c)` HAS
    `one half point under section 36A, by paragraph (4)`               IS A NUMBER
    `one half point under section 37, by paragraph (2)`                IS A NUMBER
    `points for children, by paragraphs (4), (4A), (5) and (6)`         IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `What section 66(c) gives the spouse` IS ONE OF
    `section 66(c) does not govern the spouse's calculation`
    `in a separate calculation` HAS `the credit points` IS A `Credit points under section 66(c)`

-- Version 0.2.0 (02-R2).  The refusal row IL-01 gives for s 36A and a foreign
-- worker, word for word (see the header).  The rule's name carries this row's
-- prefix, as row IL-08's does, so that it cannot collide with IL-01's rule of
-- the same words where both rows are imported together.
-- line 1811: שר האוצר רשאי לקבוע כי הוראות פרק זה לענין זיכויים, כולן או מקצתן, לא יחולו על עובד זר
@ref ITO s 48A, lines 1810-1812 — not encoded in this row
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`row IL-02, section 66(c)(4): section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"

-- (c)(4): "האשה תהא זכאית ל־½ נקודת זיכוי לפי סעיף 36א".  Half a point for the
-- woman, none for the man.  For a woman who is a foreign worker, s 48A may
-- take it away and is not encoded: declined, as row IL-01 declines s 36A
-- (its `section 36A applies to`).  A man who is a foreign worker gets 0, as
-- in IL-01: s 36A does not reach him, so s 48A cannot change the answer.
@ref s 66(c)(4), line 2465; s 36A, line 1597; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section 36A, for` `the spouse` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the spouse`'s `sex` EQUALS `a woman` AND `the spouse`'s `a foreign worker within the meaning of section 48A`
        THEN `row IL-02, section 66(c)(4): section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model`
        IF   `the spouse`'s `sex` EQUALS `a woman`
        THEN 0.5
        OTHERWISE 0

-- Version 0.3.0: the reading of fork F19 is passed to the children's points;
-- the rule of the old name, below, passes the switch.
@ref s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6), lines 2463, 2465-2478; fork F19
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      r      IS A `A reading of section 66(c)(4)(a1) for a child born before 2024`
GIVETH A `What section 66(c) gives the spouse`
`s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` which `in` couple `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` r MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (BRANCH
            IF   NOT `s 66(c) — governs the calculation of the` which `in` couple
            THEN `section 66(c) does not govern the spouse's calculation`
            IF   NOT `a woman and a man:` couple
            THEN `s 66(c)(4)-(6) speak of the woman and the man of a couple; this encoding does not decide them for a couple of the same sex`
            OTHERWISE `in a separate calculation`
                          (`Credit points under section 66(c)`
                              (`s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section 36A, for` `the spouse`)
                              (IF `the spouse`'s `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37` THEN 0.5 ELSE 0)
                              (sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` which `in` couple `for` c `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` r)
                                        (couple's `children`)))))
    WHERE
        `the spouse` MEANS `the particulars of the` which `in` couple

@ref s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6), lines 2463, 2465-2478; the switch of fork F19
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `What section 66(c) gives the spouse`
`s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` which `in` couple MEANS
    `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` which `in` couple
        `, reading an election for a child born before 2024 as` `section 66(c)(4)(a1) — the reading this row takes for an election for a child born before 2024`

-- Per spouse and provision: does the spouse have it in the separate
-- calculation?  (c)(2)'s half point under s 37 counts as having it.
-- Version 0.2.0 (02-R2): the half point under s 36A is declined for a woman
-- who is a foreign worker, as in `s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section
-- 36A, for`.  The arms of (c)(1) say who holds an entitlement in the
-- separate calculation, not whether the section gives it; whether ss 34 and 36
-- give a foreign worker points is row IL-01's count, which declines them.
@ref s 66(c)(1)-(4), lines 2461-2465; s 48A, line 1811
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      p      IS A `A provision section 66(c) speaks of`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(c) — in a separate calculation, the` which `in` couple `has the entitlement under` p MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (CONSIDER `s 66(c) — in a separate calculation, as to` p
         WHEN `each of the spouses has the entitlement`         THEN TRUE
         WHEN `one half credit point only`                      THEN (`the particulars of the` which `in` couple)'s `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`
         WHEN `there is no entitlement`                         THEN FALSE
         WHEN `the registered spouse alone has the entitlement` THEN which EQUALS `registered spouse`
         WHEN `the woman has one half credit point`             THEN
             IF   `a woman and a man:` couple
             THEN `s 66(c)(4) — the half point under section 36A, for` (`the particulars of the` which `in` couple) GREATER THAN 0
             ELSE `s 66(c)(4)-(6) speak of the woman and the man of a couple; this encoding does not decide them for a couple of the same sex`)

§§ `Section 66(c)(1A), (4), (5) — the children's points are set against the tax on income from personal exertion`

-- "ובנוסף וכנגד המס החל על הכנסתה מיגיעה אישית" ((4)); "כנגד המס החל על
-- הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית" ((5)); "כנגד המס החל על הכנסתו זו" ((1A)).  A credit
-- point is "המקוזז כנגד המס" (s 33A, line 1563).  READING (fork F13): the
-- children's points may be set only against the tax on the spouse's income
-- from personal exertion, so the credit is the lesser of their value and that
-- tax; any excess is not set against tax on other income.  The ½ point under
-- s 36A sits before "ובנוסף" and is not so confined.
--
-- The value of one credit point is s 33A's (IL-01) and the tax on income
-- from personal exertion is s 121's (IL-03): both are GIVENs, with no
-- default, because neither is a number s 66 states.
@ref s 66(c)(1A), (4), (5), lines 2462, 2465, 2473; s 33A, line 1563
GIVEN `the points for children`                                IS A NUMBER
      `the value of one credit point in the tax year`          IS A NUMBER
      `the tax on the spouse's income from personal exertion`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(c)(4)-(5) — the credit for children, set against the tax on income from personal exertion:` `the points for children` `,` `the value of one credit point in the tax year` `,` `the tax on the spouse's income from personal exertion` MEANS
    min (`the points for children` TIMES `the value of one credit point in the tax year`)
        `the tax on the spouse's income from personal exertion`
